{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1097003-kinain-c20-crossover-characters-halp","id":1097003,"title":"Kinain C20, crossover characters, Halp!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-25T23:28:41-07:00","id":1097003,"title":"Kinain C20, crossover characters, Halp!","content":"Opening Notes: Folks who get bitter about people utilizing the rules of crossover characters, may be unfit to answer these questions. Looking for answers to port over some of my old characters...for example i had a Hermetic/Satyr Kinain. With the advent of 3rd edit it was never a problem, even in M20 it wasn't really a problem. The golden rules of crossover remained the same, you may only cross a Major/Minor subgroup, and you may only have the power source of the major subgroup when making a crossover character. But then we come to C20...in 3rd edit Kinain had to be spoonfed glamour to HAVE glamour at all, so awakening was never a problem as there was no glamour in pool to stop the process of awakening for a kinain. But now in C20 Kinain regen their glamour like revenants do blood. This is flat out no bueno as regenning glamour means my character which was fine till C20 came out is now staring down the bareel of &quot;You are violating the rules of Canon for Crossover Characters&quot;. That puts me at a conundrum, I like being within canon, and I'm not interested in giving up my kinain/Mage. What should I do? Cheese that someone ravaged my kinain and he woke up in the intervening period where he didn't have glamour in pool and now quintessence rules the show? Further with how things have been borked with Kinain...How exactly does the tribe of fianna even exist? If fae and garou breed, a kinain is almost assured to be the result, and most likely a kinfolk...if that kinain/kinfolk goes on to breed with a garou, the chances are high for a kinain/Garou as that offspring (though sure it can skip generations), Now how can you have a tribe that is -fae touched- if being fae blooded entails having glamour, which would stop first change from happening? There could never be fae blooded fianna garou, because again, in C20 you're staring down the barrel of violating the cardinal rule of crossover &quot;Thou shalt not have the power sources of two supers, unless your name is Sam Haight.&quot;...so how exactly do fianna, as a tribe, exist, if all kinain have glamour and regen it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13429-joepaine","name":"JoePaine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13429_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T23:41:40-07:00","id":1097009,"title":"","content":"Color me interested, as I am in the same boat as you. It was kosher to have Kinain Garou in the old days. But I haven't read my c20 yet and I want to reveal my Wild West pack are all Kinain.<br /> <br /> <br /> Maybe if you aren't introduced to Fae society your glamour doesn't awaken and mess with things like your gnosis?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T00:03:32-07:00","id":1097015,"title":"","content":"Having a bit of glamour doesn't define your soul's destiny it may colour perceptions and shape the future paradigm but when a Mage awakens suddenly the world is different. Suddenly they are different. So for a mage with Faerie blood, I'd give them the resonance trait Dynamic(Glamour) and bonuses towards interaction with the Dreaming. Simple. IF they want more because &quot;hey my Dad's a Satyr&quot; I'd say &quot;buy blessing or Legendary attribute&quot; This even covers things like &quot;I'm pooka blooded I want to shapeshift!&quot;<br /> <br /> Glamour has even less of a say to Gaia. Those who will be her warriors will be her warriors. I Would take inspiration from the Spirit Kin Merit and apply similar effects with the Fianna who wants strong fairy blood.<br /> <br /> and if you embrace an Kinain you obviously get a DA Kiasyd but that work has already been done for you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T00:08:48-07:00","id":1097017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1097003-kinain-c20-crossover-characters-halp?p=1097009#post1097009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Color me interested, as I am in the same boat as you. It was kosher to have Kinain Garou in the old days. But I haven't read my c20 yet and I want to reveal my Wild West pack are all Kinain.<br /> <br /> <br /> Maybe if you aren't introduced to Fae society your glamour doesn't awaken and mess with things like your gnosis?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're making it needlessly complicated. Add a Point of gnosis give them afew merits. Bam.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T00:44:06-07:00","id":1097022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1097003-kinain-c20-crossover-characters-halp?p=1097015#post1097015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having a bit of glamour doesn't define your soul's destiny it may colour perceptions and shape the future paradigm but when a Mage awakens suddenly the world is different. Suddenly they are different. So for a mage with Faerie blood, I'd give them the resonance trait Dynamic(Glamour) and bonuses towards interaction with the Dreaming. Simple. IF they want more because &quot;hey my Dad's a Satyr&quot; I'd say &quot;buy blessing or Legendary attribute&quot; This even covers things like &quot;I'm pooka blooded I want to shapeshift!&quot;<br /> <br /> Glamour has even less of a say to Gaia. Those who will be her warriors will be her warriors. I Would take inspiration from the Spirit Kin Merit and apply similar effects with the Fianna who wants strong fairy blood.<br /> <br /> and if you embrace an Kinain you obviously get a DA Kiasyd but that work has already been done for you!</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is, as a satyr kinain I would already have my fathers birthright, period. I'd also already be aware of and able to interact with the dreaming and its residents as par for the course in being a satyr kinain using C20 rules. I'd just need to take off the honored birthright and an-da-shealladh fae gifts as all kinain have that now, and fae gifts are gone from kinain characters, with the birthright of a satyr kinain, needing legendary attribute would be moot Sta would already be able to hit 6. The problem I'm having is, just the glamour issue. -all- kinain have glamour from birth and it regenerates when used, if that glamour is there, The Tuatha De Danna have already spoken. As per crossover rules, with glamour in your system you can -never- awaken. So does that mean, no glamour in the moment the stressor that caused awakening occured? If so you could probably ravage a kinain and the horror of it spark an awakening, or first change. But if the whole &quot;I'm supposed to regenerat glamour and have a glamour pool&quot; means you are locked into that power source then neither garou nor mages can be fae blooded, unless the 20th rules of crossover changed as it concerns having power sources of different types of supers (which i hope that rule hasn't changed, the game doesn't need more Sam haights running about).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13429-joepaine","name":"JoePaine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13429_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T01:18:27-07:00","id":1097034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1097003-kinain-c20-crossover-characters-halp?p=1097017#post1097017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're making it needlessly complicated. Add a Point of gnosis give them afew merits. Bam.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would a Garou get extra Gnosis for being related to Fae?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T02:31:49-07:00","id":1097055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JoePaine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1097003-kinain-c20-crossover-characters-halp#post1097003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The golden rules of crossover remained the same, you may only cross a Major/Minor subgroup, and you may only have the power source of the major subgroup when making a crossover character.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think part of the problem is that this isn't actually the official &quot;golden rules&quot; in any of the books; esp. the &quot;only have one power source&quot; part. I can't find anything that says a crossover character is invalid if they'd get more than one form of supernatural juice. Perhaps that's one of those long standing house rules that you've internalized?<br /> <br /> Because without any official rule of that being the case... it stops being a problem. Your mage/kinain has Quintessence and Glamour, as benefits being both.<br /> <br /> Mage is a bit difficult to cite anything for M20, because M20 doesn't really talk about crossover characters yet.<br /> <br /> W20 however has both the Gnosis Merit, and the Supernatural Kin Merit. Neither says their are incompatible with each other in general. So there's nothing that says a mage kinfolk can't have Gnosis as well if they want to trop the 9-11 Freebies for all that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T05:14:37-07:00","id":1097081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1097003-kinain-c20-crossover-characters-halp?p=1097055#post1097055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think part of the problem is that this isn't actually the official &quot;golden rules&quot; in any of the books; esp. the &quot;only have one power source&quot; part. I can't find anything that says a crossover character is invalid if they'd get more than one form of supernatural juice. Perhaps that's one of those long standing house rules that you've internalized?<br /> <br /> Because without any official rule of that being the case... it stops being a problem. Your mage/kinain has Quintessence and Glamour, as benefits being both.<br /> <br /> Mage is a bit difficult to cite anything for M20, because M20 doesn't really talk about crossover characters yet.<br /> <br /> W20 however has both the Gnosis Merit, and the Supernatural Kin Merit. Neither says their are incompatible with each other in general. So there's nothing that says a mage kinfolk can't have Gnosis as well if they want to trop the 9-11 Freebies for all that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Officially, that 'golden rule' is more a recommendation. Gaia forgive me...Samuel Haight is proof that cross-over can happen, albeit one the demonstrates the dangers thereof.<br /> That said, I do like the idea that <b><i><u>IF</u></i></b> you are going to allow those characters in your game (always check with the ST) there is a merit buy-in and special traits come out of freebie points. It is not easy to pull off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T05:40:03-07:00","id":1097086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JoePaine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1097003-kinain-c20-crossover-characters-halp?p=1097022#post1097022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem is, as a satyr kinain I would already have my fathers birthright, period. I'd also already be aware of and able to interact with the dreaming and its residents as par for the course in being a satyr kinain using C20 rules. I'd just need to take off the honored birthright and an-da-shealladh fae gifts as all kinain have that now, and fae gifts are gone from kinain characters, with the birthright of a satyr kinain, needing legendary attribute would be moot Sta would already be able to hit 6.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A character doesn't have anything until its built. So I make a Hermetic who's background is his dad was a Satyr. He's likely of house Meridia He spends Merit points on Fae blood. He gets Glamour resonence and bonuses for interacting with the dreaming for buying the Faerie blood merit. If he wishes to have his Father's stamina he has to take legendary attribute. If he wants a bunch of fairy Gifts he buys appropriate merits and or Blessings.<br /> <br /> There is no reason he shouldn't have to use his freebies/character build to cover these powers.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The problem I'm having is, just the glamour issue. -all- kinain have glamour from birth and it regenerates when used, if that glamour is there, The Tuatha De Danna have already spoken. As per crossover rules, with glamour in your system you can -never- awaken. </div> </div> </div>This isn't true at all? Even Revenants can Awaken. Its super rare but its potential. The only thing that explicitly can't awaken are Dhampyr.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So does that mean, no glamour in the moment the stressor that caused awakening occured? If so you could probably ravage a kinain and the horror of it spark an awakening, or first change. But if the whole &quot;I'm supposed to regenerat glamour and have a glamour pool&quot; means you are locked into that power source then neither garou nor mages can be fae blooded, unless the 20th rules of crossover changed as it concerns having power sources of different types of supers (which i hope that rule hasn't changed, the game doesn't need more Sam haights running about). </div> </div> </div>Generally there are two rules of Crossover: The Abomination/Sam Haight route which is complicated and good for no one. And the DA Kiasyd, House Merita, Fianna etc route which is you get a creature of the primary genre with themes of the secondary genre. a Fianna is a werewolf but it gets gifts and potentially merits that reflect faery heretige.<br /> <br /> Kinain are written up in c20 for c20 to be a self contained book. Look at the write ups for werewolves, mages, Vampires each have &quot;glamour&quot; along with arts and realms rather than say &quot;Oh you want to use this, Lol buy awhole new game&quot; the mechanics of kinain are similarly self contained rather than intended to be the end all be all of crossover. They are intended to be used for humans with some fae blood not mechanics for Vampires with Fae blood, or Werewolves or mages.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1097003-kinain-c20-crossover-characters-halp?p=1097034#post1097034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would a Garou get extra Gnosis for being related to Fae?</div> </div> </div> </div>Its how I would represent the innate glamour. You can also go the other way and go full on &quot;they get a Birthright get to be Garou, and toss around arts, realms, Gifts and Sorcery&quot; but I personally am prone to using the Kiasyd method of crossover. You get a Creature that can completely be played in its primary Genre with themes of the secondary game.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T05:42:56-07:00","id":1097088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1097003-kinain-c20-crossover-characters-halp?p=1097081#post1097081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Officially, that 'golden rule' is more a recommendation. Gaia forgive me...Samuel Haight is proof that cross-over can happen, albeit one the demonstrates the dangers thereof.<br /> That said, I do like the idea that <b><i><u>IF</u></i></b> you are going to allow those characters in your game (always check with the ST) there is a merit buy-in and special traits come out of freebie points. It is not easy to pull off.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sam Haight is one person. There are whole groups who represent being a mixed setup that don't have this issue. They take the primary creature type and themes of the secondary.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T06:03:05-07:00","id":1097094,"title":"","content":"If the game is primarily Mage, use the Mage rules. There should be a merit called Fae-Blooded or something like that. Ignore what's in C20 and just use the merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T07:36:17-07:00","id":1097119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1097003-kinain-c20-crossover-characters-halp?p=1097088#post1097088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sam Haight is one person. There are whole groups who represent being a mixed setup that don't have this issue. They take the primary creature type and themes of the secondary.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was merely pointing out a high-profile example and that it appears tohave been used to discourge abuse. He is not representative of the whole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T10:59:48-07:00","id":1097185,"title":"","content":"Kinains always had Glamour pool. They couldn't reap it from Dreamers, but based on their Fae Blood level they could have up to 5 dots of Glamour. If I recall correctly it didn't prevent them from being a Sorcerer or Mage.<br /> <br /> BTW, Sorcerer/Kinain combo. Think about it. Can be very deadly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T13:55:37-07:00","id":1097282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1097003-kinain-c20-crossover-characters-halp?p=1097081#post1097081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Officially, that 'golden rule' is more a recommendation.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point is that &quot;golden rule&quot; or &quot;recommendation,&quot; it isn't <u>official</u>. There aren't books that present guidelines that include, &quot;don't allow character to have multiple sources of supernatural juice.&quot;<br /> <br /> The books that address such characters usually do things based on the themes and metaphysics of the different groups. Imbued Hunters can't be crossover anything. Only normal humans can Imbue, and once a character Imbues, they're cut off from becoming a mage/etc. They can potentially become vampires or wraiths or etc., but they lose all their Imbued stuff. Fera can't Awaken into mages because they're not human enough any more, but some can learn hedge magic Numina. Nothing says that a Bubasti that's learned some sorcery paths can't take the Mana background. Not just nothing as in, &quot;the rules don't explicitly say one way or the other,&quot; but the books don't even offer an opinion as a guideline most of time.<br /> <br /> That's my point. The &quot;golden rules&quot; presented in the first post aren't official guidelines, because they're not from the books.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T17:38:59-07:00","id":1097367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1097003-kinain-c20-crossover-characters-halp?p=1097119#post1097119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was merely pointing out a high-profile example and that it appears tohave been used to discourge abuse. He is not representative of the whole.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> He's even MORE doable now in v20. Abomination true hand combo that lets you borrow a Mages spheres. So he's less pure macguffin now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T00:55:23-07:00","id":1097450,"title":"","content":"...back on topic, the 'fae blooded' merit is in revised, not M20 and does say it is the same as in the Changeling book 'The Enchanted'. Assuming the 20th version is the same, the hypothetical Satyr/Heremetic would have Leagcies instead of Nature/Demeanour, a satyr birthright, the ability to see Chimera and the ability to learn (an) Art and Realms, (more than one Art if Faerie Blood Background taken)<br /> <br /> The Fae-Blooded merit states that Mage (and presumably Fera including Gaoru) cannot have a Glamour pool. Not sure how that works with the wyrd/chimeraical keywords.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T02:24:44-07:00","id":1097466,"title":"","content":"The W20 version of it doesn't say Garou/Fera can't have Glamour.<br /> <br /> And the Mage Revised one just has them use Quintessence instead of Glamour, which seems easy enough to handle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T12:02:51-07:00","id":1097579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1097003-kinain-c20-crossover-characters-halp?p=1097450#post1097450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...back on topic, the 'fae blooded' merit is in revised, not M20 and does say it is the same as in the Changeling book 'The Enchanted'. Assuming the 20th version is the same, the hypothetical Satyr/Heremetic would have Leagcies instead of Nature/Demeanour, a satyr birthright, the ability to see Chimera and the ability to learn (an) Art and Realms, (more than one Art if Faerie Blood Background taken)<br /> <br /> The Fae-Blooded merit states that Mage (and presumably Fera including Gaoru) cannot have a Glamour pool. Not sure how that works with the wyrd/chimeraical keywords.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Euthanatos have a Merit called &quot;Deathwalker&quot; in it their Spirit sphere is naturally attuned to the Underworld. They have to learn more to effect the true umbra etc. I would have Fae blooded have their spirit effects &quot;Naturally&quot; attuned towards the Dreaming. Chimerical reality is readily apparent to them like all Kinain. They can &quot;SIde step&quot; Into the Dreaming proper. They can forge Chimera with spirit. Bind them into items! All sorts of crazy stuff. And obviously give them the Resonant trait &quot;Glamour&quot;<br /> <br /> Whether your Hermetic has Legacies of Nature or Demenor really matters which you prefer. I Mean nothing in C20 is written up with Nature and Demeanor so saying &quot;they have legacies&quot; doesn't mean much. Satyr Birthright I'd buy as either Legendary Attribute or a Blessing(depending on if you are taking Stamina or Pan).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T21:33:49-07:00","id":1098345,"title":"","content":"Well, the easiest conversion would be to equate Avatar with permanent Glamour, Spheres with Arts and Realms, and Quintessence with temporary Glamour. You would keep your Banality and Fae Gifts (powered by Quintessence instead of Glamour) and be able to recover one point of Quintessence per day, up to your Avatar rating. With your low Banality and your Kinain Heritage, your Spheres should always reflect that Arts and Realms of the Changelings (regardless of your Tradition).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T00:47:36-07:00","id":1098371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1097003-kinain-c20-crossover-characters-halp?p=1097466#post1097466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The W20 version of it doesn't say Garou/Fera can't have Glamour.<br /> <br /> And the Mage Revised one just has them use Quintessence instead of Glamour, which seems easy enough to handle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}